type uses content addressing to let users build personal knowledge webs that sync peer to peer, with no server lock-in.</p><div class="mono story-card-footer"><span>↗ <!-- -->How they do it</span><span class="story-card-link">doc.anytype.io</span></div></a></div></div></div><!--astro:end--></astro-island> </div> </section> <section style="padding: 96px 32px; background: var(--pearl); border-top: 1px solid var(--hair);" data-astro-cid-sh3ffaon> <div class="mx-auto" style="max-width: 1240px;" data-astro-cid-sh3ffaon> <div style="margin-bottom: 40px; max-width: 820px;">  <h2 style="margin: 0 0 12px; font-size: var(--text-h2); font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.02em; line-height: 1.08; color: var(--navy); text-wrap: balance;"> Public, private, and everything in between </h2> <p style="margin: 0; font-size: var(--text-lead); color: var(--ink-2); max-width: 680px; line-height: 1.55;"> The same content-addressing model runs on the open internet or a closed network. Same CIDs, different routing. </p> </div> <div class="topo-grid" data-astro-cid-sh3ffaon> <!-- Public / open network --> <div class="topo-card" data-astro-cid-sh3ffaon> <div class="topo-diagram" aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-sh3ffaon> <!-- Hexagon: center (140,93) radius 68
